			"Message": "feat(Mountain): Implement regex and multiline search options in TextSearchQuery\n\nAdd missing `isRegExp` and `isMultiline` fields to TextSearchQuery, mirroring VS Code's `ITextSearchQuery` interface. When `isRegExp` is false (the default), escape the search pattern via `regex::escape()` to prevent literal searches for strings containing regex metacharacters (`.`, `(`, `[`, `*`, `?`, etc.) from crashing the regex compiler or silently matching incorrectly. Add `.multi_line()` support for multiline regex searches.\n\nThis fixes the Search view's plain-text mode which was broken for queries containing characters like `obj.method(` or `file[1].txt`.",
			"SHA": "d0117a0eb6379a9473082566dec2a8775df35577"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-24T23:05:17Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				872,
				2
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Mountain): Wire search IPC handlers to trait implementations\n\nReplace naive inline fs-walk implementations in Search.rs with delegations to the properly-implemented trait methods on MountainEnvironment:\n- `handle_search_find_in_files` → `SearchProvider::TextSearch` (grep-searcher + ignore::WalkBuilder with parallel walking)\n- `handle_search_find_files` → `WorkspaceProvider::FindFilesInWorkspace` (ignore-aware glob walker with .gitignore support)\n\nThe inline implementations had multiple deficiencies: naive `starts_with('.')` hidden-file skipping (doesn't honour .gitignore), no regex engine, bogus `format!(\"file://{}\")` URI constructor, and single-threaded walkers. The trait implementations were reachable only through `Environment.Require<dyn SearchProvider>()` calls and no IPC handler ever issued those - the \"dead code that needs to be connected\" the user flagged.\n\nAlso change FileReaddirNative.rs log level from `vfs-verbose` to `vfs` since readdir fires at most once per folder expand (unlike stat which fires per probe) and is the primary observable for Explorer view diagnostics.",
			"SHA": "5f23bca601cb496e0c86114e0aaf8db93c22cde4"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-24T21:47:23Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				872,
				4
			],
			"Message": "feat(Mountain): Add VS Code IPC command aliases and stub handlers\n\nAdd command aliases in WindServiceHandlers to bridge Mountain's native Effect-TS IPC layer with VS Code's binary IPC bridge (DiskFileSystemProviderClient, ConfigurationService):\n- Configuration: `configuration:getValue` / `configuration:updateValue` → `configuration:get` / `configuration:update`\n- File system: `file:readFile` → `file:read`, `file:writeFile` → `file:write`, `file:rename` → `file:move`\n- Add stub handlers for `file:watch` / `file:unwatch` that return Null to prevent channel promise leaks\n- Add `configuration:onDidChange` handler that acks the channel listener with Null\n\nAlso enhance Cocoon stderr filtering to suppress follow-up stack frames from extension errors (EntryNotFound, FileNotFound) that Node.js prints across multiple stderr lines. This keeps the main cocoon channel clean while routing benign extension path-probing to verbose.",
			"SHA": "661fe2405f2f71c5710b1b1e6dfb59272896fd30"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-24T21:25:18Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				872,
				4
			],
			"Message": "feat(Mountain): Fire workspaceContains and onStartupFinished extension activation\n\nImplement comprehensive startup extension activation matching VS Code's behavior:\n\n1. **Extension activation phases**: Fire three bursts at startup:\n   - `*` - unconditional activation (existing)\n   - `workspaceContains:<pattern>` - for each pattern matched by workspace\n   - `onStartupFinished` - after 2s delay for late-binding extensions\n\n2. **Pattern matching**: Add `FindMatchingWorkspaceContainsPatterns` that walks\n   workspace folders (depth 3, 4096 entries max) and matches against extension-\n   contributed `workspaceContains:` patterns using a minimal glob matcher.\n\n3. **Stderr filtering**: Downgrade benign Node.js/macOS noise to `cocoon-stderr-verbose`:\n   - macOS codesign messages (\"is already signed\", \"replacing existing signature\")\n   - Node deprecation warnings (DeprecationWarning, --trace-deprecation)\n   - Keeps main cocoon channel clean for actionable errors only.\n\n4. **Rust edition**: Upgrade from 2021 to 2024.\n\nThis fixes extensions that never activated without user interaction because they\ngate on `workspaceContains:package.json`, `onStartupFinished`, or similar events.",
			"SHA": "72db08550a3a7b20669947fe3bac64deb2e0300d"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-24T20:52:00Z",
			"File": [
				"⠁⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				872,
				11
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Mountain): Move high-frequency logging to verbose/opt-in tags\n\nContinue reducing default log volume by routing per-operation lines to dedicated verbose tags that are muted in `short` mode:\n\n1. **Command registration**: `commands` → `commands-verbose` for setContext (~130/session) and command execution in CommandProvider\n2. **Output channels**: `grpc` → `output-verbose` for append/create events (200+ appends per boot from language servers)\n3. **Command registry**: `grpc` → `command-register` for register/unregister notifications (~100 commands/session)\n4. **Provider registration**: `grpc`/extensions → `grpc-verbose`/`provider-register` for duplicate provider registration logs\n5. **Extension scanning**: `extensions` → `ext-scan-verbose` for per-candidate package.json probes (203/session)\n6. **Scheme assets**: `lifecycle` → `scheme-assets` for per-asset vscode-file:// requests (worker/wasm/font loading)\n\nNew tags added to SHORT_MODE_MUTED_TAGS: output-verbose, command-register, provider-register, ext-scan-verbose, channel-stub, commands-verbose, scheme-assets.",
			"SHA": "7d046f166e341789c3445eb14c727db2ed044a11"
		}
	],
